# Write the first chapter

The screen has two halves. You write on the left, and the right shows the page as a reader will see it.

1. Select all the sample text on the left and delete it.
2. Type a heading on the first line, starting with `#` and a space.
3. Leave a blank line, then write a paragraph or two.

For example:

``` djot
# The Storm

The wind rose after dark, and by midnight the waves were breaking over the rocks.

Anna climbed the stairs to light the lamp.
```

The preview changes as you type. The heading becomes the chapter's name in the book's contents, so give every chapter one.

A blank line starts a new paragraph. To make a word _italic_, put underscores around it: `_italic_`. For *bold*, use asterisks: `*bold*`.

There is no Save button. SEED.html saves the chapter as you write.
